{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"6a8e5dc1-fc3d-40be-b9af-983adc609ecc","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A string fixed at both ends can form a standing wave. These two curves show opposite extremes of the same vibration.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Standing waves on a string"},{"op":"diagram","id":"string","region":"right","primitives":[{"kind":"line","points":[[0.1,0.5],[0.9,0.5]],"stroke":"dashed","meaning":"equilibrium position of the string"},{"kind":"smooth","points":[[0.1,0.5],[0.3,0.25],[0.5,0.5],[0.7,0.75],[0.9,0.5]],"stroke":"solid","meaning":"string displacement at one extreme"},{"kind":"smooth","points":[[0.1,0.5],[0.3,0.75],[0.5,0.5],[0.7,0.25],[0.9,0.5]],"stroke":"dashed","meaning":"string displacement half a period later"},{"kind":"line","points":[[0.1,0.4],[0.1,0.6]],"stroke":"solid","meaning":"fixed left endpoint"},{"kind":"line","points":[[0.9,0.4],[0.9,0.6]],"stroke":"solid","meaning":"fixed right endpoint"}],"tension":0.55}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"6a8e5dc1-fc3d-40be-b9af-983adc609ecc","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Nodes never move. Here, both fixed ends and the center remain at zero displacement throughout the vibration.","ops":[{"op":"point","id":"nodeleft","canvas_id":"string","at":[0.1,0.5],"label":"N"},{"op":"point","id":"nodecenter","canvas_id":"string","at":[0.5,0.5],"label":"N"},{"op":"point","id":"noderight","canvas_id":"string","at":[0.9,0.5],"label":"N"},{"op":"text","id":"nodedef","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"Node: zero motion"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"6a8e5dc1-fc3d-40be-b9af-983adc609ecc","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Antinodes lie halfway between neighboring nodes. These points move most, swinging between the upper and lower extremes.","ops":[{"op":"arrow","id":"antileft","canvas_id":"string","from":[0.3,0.75],"to":[0.3,0.25],"stroke":"solid","label":"A"},{"op":"arrow","id":"antiright","canvas_id":"string","from":[0.7,0.25],"to":[0.7,0.75],"stroke":"solid","label":"A"},{"op":"text","id":"antidef","anchor":{"el":"nodedef","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"Antinode: maximum motion"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"At the center node, does the string ever move up or down?","expected_gist":"No. A node stays at zero displacement at all times."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"6a8e5dc1-fc3d-40be-b9af-983adc609ecc","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Neighboring nodes are half a wavelength apart. A node and its nearest antinode are one quarter wavelength apart.","ops":[{"op":"line","id":"nodespan","canvas_id":"string","from":[0.1,0.86],"to":[0.5,0.86],"stroke":"solid","label":"λ/2"},{"op":"line","id":"quarterspan","canvas_id":"string","from":[0.5,0.16],"to":[0.7,0.16],"stroke":"solid","label":"λ/4"},{"op":"equation","id":"spacing","anchor":{"el":"antidef","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"d_{NN}=\\frac{\\lambda}{2},\\qquad d_{NA}=\\frac{\\lambda}{4}"}],"checkpoint":null}}
